# Commands a skill names but never runs, so they need no grant.
# One row per command: <skill>|<command prefix>|<reason>. Keep the reason
# specific; lint-tools fails on a row that no longer matches anything.
api-versioning|make test-contracts|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
company-attribution|make check|the gate the skill adds headers-check to
license-compliance|make licenses|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
license-compliance|npm ci|named as a reproducible-build flag in the release notes
license-compliance|uv sync --frozen|named as a reproducible-build flag in the release notes
secrets|make env-check|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
doctor|make setup|run only inside a throwaway clone to reproduce, never in the user's clone
doctor|git update-index|a fix line printed for the engineer
doctor|npm install|named as the step that resets core.hooksPath, never run
gate-audit|git ls-files|an example of a gate pattern that passes on empty input
mcp-server|claude mcp add|a registration line printed for the user
postmortem|git log|output the caller pasted; the skill reads it, never runs it
release|npm i|a README install line the skill greps for
release|pnpm add|a README install line the skill greps for
release|go get|a README install line the skill greps for
workflow|git init|a next action named for the engineer
docs-drift|make test|a docs claim the skill checks against the recipe, never runs
